  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So, ever since the latest game update on VRChat, I've been experiencing this bug with my in-game movement. However, this issue only occurs when playing the PC-VR version (Quest 2 + Virtual Desktop).\n\nI find myself automatically moving backward. A friend of mine suggested it might be \"drifting\" caused by mechanical problems in the Quest controller. To test this theory, I tried playing the standalone Quest version, and the drifting didn't occur. This suggests it's not a hardware issue but rather a software bug.\n\nAdditionally, it's worth noting that every time I launch the game in PC-VR mode, the \"Flick\" option on the settings wheel is disabled, and I have to manually enable it. There might be some connection between this and the drifting bug, as both problems started simultaneously after the last game update.\n\nCan you guys help me out?",
